    {
        cmd: "idioms"
        title: "Search with rg, find with fd, pick with tv"
        use: "Nothing to run — four rules that stop an agent guessing. Search with `rg` and find with `fd`, never `grep`/`find`. Pick with television (`tv`) — the single exception is `zi`/`cdi`, which open fzf, and it is the only place fzf belongs. Nushell commands return structured data, so filter with `| where`, not `| grep`. And `cd` here can create the directory it is given."
        topic: "agents"
        task: "agents"
