    {
        cmd: "cll [model]"
        title: "Start Claude Code on a chosen model"
        use: "Run `cll` with no argument and a picker opens, grouped by provider; pick a row and Claude Code starts on that model. `cll <model>` skips the picker. Rows named `native:*` bypass the proxy and run on the Max plan; everything else goes through the local proxy with its fallback chain. The picked model's context window is declared at launch, so auto-compact fires against what the model actually serves — 1M stays 1M instead of compacting at 200K."
        topic: "agents"
        task: "agents"
        step: 3
        mode: "shell"
        also: ["llm", "llm quota"]
        why: "The picker lives in the script rather than in the shell, so every shell gets the same one. An earlier split — a nushell picker calling a script launcher — meant a stale shell called the script with no model at all and fell into a fallback path nothing had ever exercised."
        verify: [{kind: "command", name: "cll"}]
        source: "prds/04-shell/10-litellm-launcher/prd.md"
    }
    {
        cmd: "llm"
        title: "See every model and what is left on it"
        use: "Run `llm` for the catalogue as a table: every model, who serves it, and the balance remaining. It is a nushell table, so `llm | where provider == openai` works."
        topic: "agents"
        task: "agents"
        step: 4
        mode: "shell"
        also: ["cll [model]", "llm quota", "llm regen"]
        why: "One table rather than a page per provider: choosing a model is a comparison, and a comparison wants rows."
        verify: [{kind: "command", name: "llm"}]
        source: "prds/04-shell/10-litellm-launcher/prd.md"
    }
    {
        cmd: "llm quota"
        title: "Read or record the balance per provider"
        use: "`llm quota` prints the balances. `llm quota refresh` re-fetches the ones that have an API; `llm quota set <provider> <amount>` records the ones only a dashboard can tell you."
        topic: "agents"
        task: "agents"
        step: 5
        mode: "shell"
        also: ["llm", "cll [model]"]
        why: "Two kinds of provider, one command: some publish a balance endpoint and some publish nothing at all, and the second kind is why `set` exists rather than an empty column."
        verify: [{kind: "command", name: "llm quota"}]
        source: "prds/04-shell/10-litellm-launcher/prd.md"
    }
    {
        cmd: "llm regen"
        title: "Rebuild the proxy's routing from live inventories"
        use: "Run `llm regen` after a provider gains or loses models: it rewrites the proxy's routing config from what the providers actually serve now, and tells you to restart the proxy to pick it up."
        topic: "agents"
        task: "agents"
        step: 6
        mode: "shell"
        also: ["llm", "cll [model]"]
        why: "The routing config is derived, never hand-edited — a hand-edited route outlives the model it names and fails at the moment you most want the model."
        verify: [{kind: "command", name: "llm regen"}]
